h or success to a  success there's always a lot of other  people in the background doing a lot of  the work that this person is you know  taking credit for and has been fortunate  enough to be in that position don't  judge yourself  and how you're doing based on what you  see other people who appear to be  successful doing until you actually  spend time with them and know them it's  enough if you make some progress in you  know reading books or exercising your  body to be more healthy or working on  your relationships or developing some  philosophical or spiritual practices  that you do that you find improve your  life that's that's good that's actually  doing something for yourself and if you  prioritize if you order your life to  provide those space and time and energy  and thought within your life you will  you will find like people have  throughout these centuries and Millennia  that you know you derive some reward  from it and it doesn't have to be you  know Earth shaking it doesn't have to be  insights all the time it doesn't have to  be benching 450 pounds or you know  squatting and doing this or any sort of  craziness like that in order for you to  have actually  achieved something  you can indeed make a lot of progress  but you know it requires attentiveness  it requires deliberately choosing these  things over and over and over again you  can't make a choice once or a plan or a  schedule and then it just falls into  place you have to keep on persevering in  that and that's tough and so you know I  I feel for all of you out there who are  trying to do that because I've been  there myself and I still fail at you  know setting up good priorities for  myself that I can stick to  consistently I fail myself day by day  week by week but you just keep working  at it and eventually you get a bit  better at it but you don't have to try  to do everything you shouldn't place  that pressure upon yourself the key if  you do have to do anything this is the  last bit of a